        "Charles L. Sawyers"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition established molecularly targeted therapy as a highly effective treatment paradigm for chronic myeloid leukemia.",
        "attribution": "Lydon contributed critically to inhibitor development, Druker to clinical translation, and Sawyers to the disease-mechanistic and resistance framework.",
        "maturity": "The clinical impact, mechanism, and general influence on cancer therapeutics are firmly mature.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit is distributed across target discovery, drug discovery, and clinical development."
        ]
      }
    },
