        "Michael J. Welsh",
        "Fred Van Goor",
        "Paul A. Negulescu"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Functional rescue of mutant CFTR converted cystic fibrosis from a largely symptomatic-treatment condition toward mechanism-based therapy.",
        "attribution": "Welsh provided key CFTR functional biology, while Van Goor and Negulescu are strongly associated with translating pharmacologic modulation into treatment.",
        "maturity": "Clinical gains from CFTR modulators are substantial and sustained, with a direct mechanistic link to the disease defect.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery and development chain contains many essential contributors and varies by CFTR mutation."
        ]
      }
    },
