        "Terje Lømo",
        "Timothy V. P. Bliss",
        "Richard G. M. Morris"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Long-term potentiation provided a durable experimental framework for activity-dependent synaptic change and learning-related plasticity.",
        "attribution": "Lømo and Bliss established the phenomenon, and Morris made influential connections between synaptic plasticity and memory.",
        "maturity": "Its cellular mechanisms and relevance to neural plasticity have been investigated across many preparations and decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Whether LTP alone constitutes the synaptic basis of learning and memory remains an important conceptual limitation."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
